On Wed, 18 Aug 2004 09:31:45 -0400, Christopher T King wrote:

> I learned from a recent post here how easy it is to tame new (domestic) 
> pets, and have been experimenting with having multiple pets.  Are there 
> any downsides to this, or is this an all-around good idea (especially for 
> weak characters)?  I imagine chaotics lose some alignment points, and too 
> many pets killing and eating things will prevent you from being able to do 
> the same, but are there any more things to be wary of?

Chaotics only lose alignment by healing their pets, not from having them.
I can state from personal experience that the more cats you have the more
chaos you generate. In chaotic character, I like to have multiple pets in 
the mines because they find the traps more quickly, and you have more
things to whistle onto onto polytraps. (In the mines, every pet is a
guinea pig.)

The major disadvantages to having multiple pets are diet conflicts (unless
you're staying vegetarian or have poison resistance), herding everyone
together at stairs, and trying to loot a shop with more than one pet
inside. I've had several instances trying to do this, where one pet
dropped an item right in front of me and the next pet took it back into
the shop before I'd moved.

Just remember also to keep track of where all your pets are before using
wands of magic missile, etc. 

